    "final_message": "The red acceptance tests now pass. `scripts/verify story-drafting` came back green on its first run: tessercheck found nothing, `mypy --strict` passed, 79 non-root tests passed, and both acceptance tests passed against the host on :9340. Only the four files that are mine changed, and they're committed as `45f80af` on the worktree branch.\n\n**Domain** (`<repo>/story-drafting/drafting/domain/jtbd.py`):\n- **`Text`** now refuses blank input, which is what guarantees every story has a non-empty given, when and then.\n- **`StoryText`** is a new value object built from `StoryTextSpec`. Its `drafted()` turns it into a `StoryView` in state drafted.\n- **`StoryTexts`** is a new collection value object built from `RecordStoriesSpec`. I added these two so the spec's fields are only read inside the constructor that takes them, which is the TB083 rule.\n- **`Jtbd.record_stories`** answers `ALREADY_RECORDED` if the job to be done already has stories and `NONE_GIVEN` if no story texts come in. Otherwise it keeps each text as a drafted story and answers `RECORDED`.\n- **`Jtbd.status`** is worked out from the stories rather than stored: no stories gives `drafting_stories`, any drafted story gives `awaiting_story_acceptance`, and otherwise it's `stories_decided`.\n- **Contract:** every public signature is as the stub had it.\n- **Tests:** `test_jtbd.py` covers each status, each of the three outcomes, that a recorded story comes back drafted, and that blank text is refused.\n\n**Drafter** (`<repo>/story-drafting/drafting/adapters/gateways/template_story_drafter.py`): it always fills the same two templates with the request's `role`, `i_want` and `so_that`:\n- \"I am {role}\" / \"I want {i_want}\" / \"it is done, so that {so_that}\"\n- the same job after stepping away and coming back, ending \"I find it where I left it, so that {so_that}\"\n\nIts tests check that i"
